qa-dashboard (0.5.9) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Add QA Sentinels 1.3.0 network and connectivity query categories.
  * Refresh companion metadata for the new Sentinels implementation.
  * Rebuild the normal and diagnostics pre-release packages.
  * Allow resizing and maximizing the Logs window.
  * Keep the focused QA window in front when the generic launcher is clicked
    instead of always raising Overview.
  * Open the main Dashboard on Shift+click of the QA launcher icon.
  * Sync the vendored QA Sentinels tree to 1.4.1 (c9ac41f) and add a vendor
    alignment check. Windows and macOS bundles now include the engine; Linux
    keeps the external qa-sentinels package and does not bundle it.
  * Follow the configured Sentinels root for the Tickets window.
  * Only show the layer-2 deep journal when it belongs to the configured
    Sentinels workspace.
  * Skip rasdaemon probes on desktops without CXL hardware and still collect
    EDAC, AER, APEI and pstore state.
  * Preserve the consented LinkedIn URL when staging tickets instead of
    redacting the username inside it.
  * Rename the ticket summary heading from "What happens" to "Description".
  * Add optional reporter identity fields to QA Sentinels Settings. Linux
    reads the existing workspace identity; Windows and macOS start empty.
  * Ship the hidden GNOME Shell helper in the APT package and enable it on
    first login, restoring Shift+click on the QA launcher.
  * Stop desktop notifications for draft tickets; draft generation stays
    silent while raise and ready-correlation alerts remain.
  * Add a Ctrl+F find bar scoped to the Logs output, with match navigation
    and retained keyboard focus.
  * Sync the vendored QA Sentinels tree to 1.4.2 (5bcfa80), including the
    optional crash-feed ingestion, stored crash component labels, warning
    findings for non-critical kernel conditions, the complete rule register,
    the host-aligned security-policy example, child user-namespace
    capability scoping, setuid-helper exe fallback, and no-coredump
    preflight handling.
  * Add a Rules action to the left of Documentation and render the complete
    QA Sentinels rule register from docs/RULES.md in the Documentation page
    style. Rules stays visible in Overview and is hidden with Documentation
    in Tickets. The Dashboard copy keeps the portable platform section marked
    WIP.
  * Remove the QA Sentinels prefix from the Documentation and Rules page
    headers.
  * Keep the generated Rules page aligned with the shortened "Rules" header
    and the Dashboard rule-register copy.
  * Remove the implementation summary from the Documentation page.

 -- Gerard Sala <creative.gsp@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100

